/E (Students from various colleges and universities visited The Ability People as part of their academic projects to gain firsthand exposure to the functioning of a non-governmental organization. They interacted with our team and beneficiaries, learning about our rehabilitation programmes, community initiatives, and the impact of inclusive services. Curious to understand the journey of an NGO from the ground up, they explored how projects are conceptualized, funds are mobilized, resources are managed, and programmes are implemented. The visit fostered meaningful discussions, practical learning, and a deeper appreciation for the role of NGOs in creating sustainable social impact.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
